test_failure*úUnit testing: assertions, test-case/test-suite registration, and a
runner. See spec/specification/04-stdlib/testing/61-std-test.md.
An assertion failure: either a bare message, or an expected/actual
mismatch with both sides already rendered to `str`.:Q
assert_true*>Succeeds iff `cond` is `true`; otherwise fails with `message`.:S
assert_false*?Succeeds iff `cond` is `false`; otherwise fails with `message`.:m
	assert_eq*\Succeeds iff `actual == expected`; otherwise fails with a rendered
expected/actual mismatch.:m
	assert_ne*\Succeeds iff `actual != expected`; otherwise fails with a rendered
expected/actual mismatch.:(
fail*Always fails with `message`.:n
	test_case*]One test to run: a name, the function to call, and whether the runner
should skip calling it.:7
case*+Builds an ordinary (non-skipped) test case.:W
skipped*HBuilds a test case the runner reports as skipped, without calling `run`.:œ

test_suite*‰A named group of test cases with optional once-per-suite
(`before_all`/`after_all`) and once-per-case (`before_each`/`after_each`)
hooks.:ˆ
suite*{Builds a `test_suite`. Every hook defaults to `@none`, so a suite that
needs none of them passes only a name and its cases.:A
render_failure*+Renders a `test_failure` for a report line.:N
report*@Prints one report line for `name` and returns whether it passed.:¼
run*°Runs every case in `cases` in order (skipping `skip: true` ones), with no
suite-level hooks and no per-suite name in the report. Equivalent to
`run_suites([suite("", cases)])`.:z

run_suites*hRuns every suite in order and prints a report; returns `0` if every case
and hook passed, `1` otherwise.